# What NOT to commit from the generated iOS project.
#
# The tree is tracked so Xcode Cloud has a project to build (it builds from
# the repository, not from the machine that generated it) — but most of what
# `./buddy build:ios` writes here is reproducible and does not belong in git.

# Swift is restored on the build machine from the locked Craft package by
# ci_scripts/ci_post_clone.sh, so committing it would pin a copy that the
# next framework bump silently contradicts.
#
# ⚠️ scripts/patch-ios-tabbar.ts REWRITES THESE FILES, and an Xcode Cloud
# build regenerates them after the checkout — so the squared tab-bar
# highlight does NOT survive that path. It is applied for local and e2e
# builds, where the runner patches between generation and compile. Retire
# both when craft-native/craft#386 ships a real option.
*.swift

# The compiler's copy of the screens; dist/ carries the one that ships.
/native-screens.js
/native-screens/
